mechanism:
The four standalone patterns
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2bf16_rn f32:$a),      (CVT_bf16_f32 $a, CvtRN)>;
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2bf16_rn_relu ...), (CVT_bf16_f32 ... CvtRN_RELU)>;
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2bf16_rz ...),      (CVT_bf16_f32 ... CvtRZ)>;
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2bf16_rz_relu ...), (CVT_bf16_f32 ... CvtRZ_RELU)>;
have no pattern-level guard. CVT_bf16_f32 is the _f32 def of CVT_FROM_ALL<"bf16"> (NVPTXInstrInfo.td:580-587) whose ToType==bf16 branch sets Requires<[hasPTX<70>, hasSM<80>]> with the comment "f32->bf16 was introduced early" — i.e. exactly sm_80. Because the patterns are standalone, that instruction Requires does not gate the match, so cvt.{rn,rz}[.relu].bf16.f32 is emitted on pre-sm_80 targets. ptxas rejects: scalar .bf16 conversions require .target sm_80 (PTX ISA 7.0). The sibling f2bf16 satfinite patterns (lines 2145-2150) are correctly wrapped in let Predicates=[hasPTX<81>,hasSM<80>], confirming the intended guard is missing on the non-satfinite ones.

