mechanism:
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2f16_rn_relu f32:$a), (CVT_f16_f32 $a, CvtRN_RELU)>;
  def : Pat<(int_nvvm_f2f16_rz_relu f32:$a), (CVT_f16_f32 $a, CvtRZ_RELU)>;
have no pattern-level predicate. Although CVT_f16_f32 (scalar f32->f16) itself is an old/valid sm_53 instruction, the CvtRN_RELU/CvtRZ_RELU operand makes the printer emit the `.relu` saturation modifier (`cvt.rn.relu.f16.f32`). The `.relu` cvt saturation modifier (RELU_FLAG) was introduced in PTX ISA 7.0 for sm_80 (added by reviews.llvm.org/D116673, all of whose new modes Require<[hasPTX70,hasSM80]>). Emitting `cvt.rn.relu.f16.f32` on .version 4.2/sm_53 is therefore rejected by ptxas (`.relu` not recognized for this target). The plain (non-relu) f2f16 patterns are fine; only the relu ones are invalid below sm_80.

